[ERR] 2026-01-22 17:38:00 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/LSTTN_ADAPTATION_DOCUMENTATION.md', 'content': '# LSTTN Model Adaptation Documentation\n\n## Overview\nThis document describes the adaptation of the LSTTN (Long Short-Term Transformer Network) model from its original implementation to LibCity framework conventions.\n\n## Original Implementation\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/liuxu77/LSTTN\n- **Paper**: "LSTTN: Long Short-Term Transformer Network for Spatiotemporal Traffic Forecasting"\n- **Original Files**:\n  - `repos/LSTTN/models/lsttn.py` - Main LSTTN class\n  - `repos/LSTTN/models/transformer.py` - Long-term transformer encoder\n  - `repos/LSTTN/models/graph_wavenet.py` - Short-term GraphWaveNet\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n### Components\n1. **Long-term Component**: Masked transformer with dilated convolutions\n   - Processes 14 days of historical data (4032 timesteps at 5-min intervals)\n   - Extracts long-term trends and seasonal patterns (weekly/daily)\n   - Uses patch-based encoding with learnable positional embeddings\n\n2. **Short-term Component**: GraphWaveNet with adaptive graph convolution\n   - Processes recent 1 hour of data (12 timesteps at 5-min intervals)\n   - Captures short-term spatial-temporal dynamics\n   - Uses dilated causal convolutions with adaptive adjacency learning\n\n3. **Fusion Module**: MLP-based trend-seasonality fusion\n   - Combines long-term trends, seasonality, and short-term patterns\n   - Produces final multi-step predictions\n\n## Key Adaptations for LibCity\n\n### 1. Base Class Integration\n**Original**: `class LSTTN(nn.Module)`\n**Adapted**: `class LSTTN(AbstractTrafficStateModel)`\n\nInherited from LibCity\'s `AbstractTrafficStateModel` base class to ensure compatibility with LibCity\'s training and evaluation pipeline.\n\n### 2. Data Format Transformation\n\n#### Input Format\n**Original**:\n- Two separate inputs: `short_x` and `long_x`\n- `short_x`: (batch_size, 12, num_nodes, num_features)\n- `long_x`: (batch_size, 4032, num_nodes, num_features)\n\n**Adapted**:\n- Single input: `batch[\'X\']`\n- Shape: (batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n- Short sequence extracted from last 12 timesteps\n- Long sequence handling:\n  - When `use_long_term=True` and sufficient history available: use first `long_seq_len` timesteps\n  - Otherwise: only use short-term component\n\n#### Output Format\n**Original**: (batch_size, num_nodes, pre_len)\n**Adapted**: (batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)\n\nTransposed and reshaped to match LibCity\'s expected output format.\n\n### 3. Configuration Management\n\n**Original**: Model initialized with nested config dictionaries and keyword arguments\n```python\nLSTTN(cfg, **model_args)\n```\n\n**Adapted**: Flat config dictionary following LibCity conventions\n```python\nLSTTN(config, data_feature)\n```\n\nAll hyperparameters extracted from `config` dict with sensible defaults:\n- `input_window`, `output_window` - Sequence lengths\n- `use_long_term` - Enable/disable long-term component\n- `transformer_*` - Transformer hyperparameters\n- `gwnet_*` - GraphWaveNet hyperparameters\n- `*_hidden_dim` - Component dimensions\n\n### 4. Data Feature Integration\n\nExtracted from `data_feature` dict:\n- `num_nodes` - Number of nodes in graph\n- `feature_dim` - Number of input features per node\n- `output_dim` - Number of output features per node\n- `adj_mx` - Adjacency matrix (converted to transition matrices)\n- `scaler` - Data normalization scaler\n\n### 5. Loss Function\n\n**Original**: Custom loss implementation\n**Adapted**: Uses LibCity\'s `loss.masked_mae_torch`\n\n```python\ndef calculate_loss(self, batch):\n    y_true = batch[\'y\']\n    y_predicted = self.predict(batch)\n    y_true = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_true[..., :self.output_dim])\n    y_predicted = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_predicted[..., :self.output_dim])\n    return loss.masked_mae_torch(y_predicted, y_true, 0)\n```\n\nPerforms inverse scaling before loss calculation to evaluate on original scale.\n\n### 6. Pretrained Transformer Support\n\n**Original**: Hardcoded loading from specific paths based on dataset name\n```python\nif self.dataset_name == "METRLA":\n    state_dict = torch.load("../pretrained_transformers/METR-LA.pt")\n```\n\n**Adapted**: Configurable path via `pretrained_transformer_path` parameter\n```python\nself.pretrained_transformer_path = config.get(\'pretrained_transformer_path\', None)\nif self.pretrained_transformer_path is not None:\n    self._load_pretrained_transformer()\n```\n\n### 7. Adjacency Matrix Processing\n\n**Original**: Expects supports list passed directly\n**Adapted**: Converts LibCity\'s adjacency matrix to forward/backward transition matrices\n\n```python\ndef _prepare_supports(self):\n    # Convert adjacency to transition matrices\n    adj_forward = D^{-1} * A\n    adj_backward = D^{-1} * A^T\n    return [adj_forward, adj_backward]\n```\n\n## Important Implementation Notes\n\n### Long-term Sequence Handling\nThe original LSTTN requires 14 days of historical data (4032 timesteps). LibCity\'s default dataset loaders may not provide this much history. We handle this in two ways:\n\n1. **Recommended**: Set `use_long_term=False` to use only the short-term GraphWaveNet component\n   - Works with standard LibCity input_window (e.g., 12 timesteps)\n   - Still achieves good performance\n\n2. **Full Model**: Set `use_long_term=True` and ensure dataset provides long history\n   - Requires modifying dataset configuration to load more historical timesteps\n   - Provides best performance by leveraging long-term patterns\n\n### Model Components Preserved\n\nAll original model components are preserved with minimal changes:\n- `InputEmbedding` - Patch-based embedding for long sequences\n- `LearnableTemporalPositionalEncoding` - Learnable positional encoding\n- `TransformerLayers` - Standard transformer encoder\n- `StackedDilatedConv` - Dilated convolutions for trend extraction\n- `DynamicGraphConv` - Graph convolution with adaptive adjacency\n- `GraphWaveNet` - Complete short-term spatio-temporal model\n\n### Dimension Handling\n\nThe model automatically handles dimension mismatches:\n- If `input_window < short_seq_len`: pads with zeros\n- If `input_window >= long_seq_len` and `use_long_term=True`: uses long-term component\n- GraphWaveNet uses only first 2 features (following original implementation)\n\n## Configuration Example\n\n### Minimal Configuration (Short-term Only)\n```json\n{\n    "model": "LSTTN",\n    "input_window": 12,\n    "output_window": 12,\n    "use_long_term": false\n}\n```\n\n### Full Configuration (With Long-term)\n```json\n{\n    "model": "LSTTN",\n    "input_window": 4032,  # Must include long history\n    "output_window": 12,\n    "use_long_term": true,\n    "short_seq_len": 12,\n    "long_seq_len": 4032,\n    "pretrained_transformer_path": "path/to/pretrained/transformer.pt",\n    "transformer_patch_size": 12,\n    "transformer_out_channel": 64,\n    "transformer_num_layers": 4,\n    "gwnet_residual_channels": 32,\n    "gwnet_end_channels": 512\n}\n```\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import LSTTN\n\n# Configuration\nconfig = {\n    \'input_window\': 12,\n    \'output_window\': 12,\n    \'use_long_term\': False,\n    \'device\': torch.device(\'cuda\'),\n}\n\n# Data features\ndata_feature = {\n    \'num_nodes\': 207,\n    \'feature_dim\': 3,\n    \'output_dim\': 1,\n    \'adj_mx\': adj_matrix,\n    \'scaler\': standard_scaler,\n}\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = LSTTN(config, data_feature)\n\n# Forward pass\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.randn(32, 12, 207, 3),  # (batch, time, nodes, features)\n    \'y\': torch.randn(32, 12, 207, 1),  # (batch, time, nodes, features)\n}\npredictions = model.predict(batch)  # (32, 12, 207, 1)\n\n# Calculate loss\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n```\n\n## Testing\n\nA test script is provided to verify the model works correctly:\n```bash\npython test_lsttn_import.py\n```\n\nThis will:\n1. Import the LSTTN model\n2. Initialize with test configuration\n3. Run a forward pass with dummy data\n4. Verify output shapes\n\n## Files Modified/Created\n\n### Created\n- `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/LSTTN.py` - Main model implementation\n\n### Modified\n- `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py` - Added LSTTN import and registration\n\n### Documentation\n- `test_lsttn_import.py` - Test script\n- `LSTTN_config_template.json` - Configuration template\n- This documentation file\n\n## Known Limitations and Future Work\n\n1. **Long-term Component**: Requires large input_window (4032 timesteps)\n   - May need dataset loader modifications\n   - Consider implementing sliding window approach\n\n2. **Pretrained Transformer**: Original paper uses pretrained weights\n   - Not included in this adaptation\n   - Users can train their own or disable long-term component\n\n3. **Memory Usage**: Full model (with long-term) is memory-intensive\n   - Recommend using short-term only for initial experiments\n   - Consider gradient checkpointing for large-scale training\n\n4. **Graph Structure**: Currently uses transition matrices\n   - Could explore other graph normalization schemes\n   - May benefit from learned graph structures\n\n## References\n\n1. Original Paper: [Add paper link when available]\n2. Original Code: https://github.com/liuxu77/LSTTN\n3. LibCity Framework: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n\n## Contact\n\nFor questions or issues related to this adaptation, please refer to the LibCity documentation or open an issue in the repository.\n'}
