itecture Overview\n\n### Original LSTTN Components\n1. **Long-term Transformer** (14 days history)\n   - Patch-based encoding (patch_size=12)\n   - Learnable positional encoding\n   - Multi-layer transformer encoder (4 layers, 64 hidden dim)\n   - Dilated convolutions for trend extraction (128 hidden dim)\n   - Dynamic graph convolution for seasonality (64 hidden dim each for weekly/daily)\n\n2. **Short-term GraphWaveNet** (1 hour history)\n   - Adaptive graph learning\n   - Dilated causal convolutions\n   - 4 blocks × 2 layers\n   - Skip connections and residual connections\n\n3. **Fusion Module**\n   - MLP-based combination of long/short-term features\n   - Final projection to prediction horizon\n\n### Adapted for LibCity\n\n**Input**:\n- `batch[\'X\']`: (batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n- Single unified input (instead of separate short/long inputs)\n\n**Output**:\n- (batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)\n- Matches LibCity\'s expected format\n\n**Key Adaptations**:\n1. Extract short sequence from last 12 timesteps of batch[\'X\']\n2. Use full sequence as long sequence when available and use_long_term=True\n3. Support flexible input_window (not restricted to 4032+12)\n4. Configurable long-term component (can be disabled)\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Essential Parameters\n- `input_window`: 12 (or 4032 for long-term)\n- `output_window`: 12\n- `use_long_term`: false (true if long history available)\n\n### Transformer Parameters (Long-term)\n- `transformer_patch_size`: 12\n- `transformer_in_channel`: 1\n- `transformer_out_channel`: 64\n- `transformer_num_layers`: 4\n- `transformer_dropout`: 0.1\n\n### GraphWaveNet Parameters (Short-term)\n- `gwnet_residual_channels`: 32\n- `gwnet_dilation_channels`: 32\n- `gwnet_skip_channels`: 256\n- `gwnet_end_channels`: 512\n- `gwnet_kernel_size`: 2\n- `gwnet_blocks`: 4\n- `gwnet_layers`: 2\n\n### Model Architecture Parameters\n- `long_trend_hidden_dim`: 128\n- `seasonality_hidden_dim`: 64\n- `mlp_hidden_dim`: 128\n- `dropout`: 0.3\n\n---\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\n### 1. Dual-Input Handling\n**Challenge**: Original model expects separate short (12-step) and long (4032-step) inputs\n\n**Solution**:\n```python\n# Extract short sequence from last 12 timesteps\nif input_len >= self.short_seq_len:\n    short_x = x[:, -self.short_seq_len:, :, :]\nelse:\n    # Pad if necessary\n    short_x = F.pad(x, (0, 0, 0, 0, pad_len, 0))\n\n# Use full sequence as long sequence when available\nif self.use_long_term and input_len >= self.long_seq_len:\n    long_x = x[:, :self.long_seq_len, :, :]\n```\n\n### 2. Flexible Long-term Component\n**Feature**: Can enable/disable long-term modeling based on data availability\n\n```python\nif self.use_long_term and input_len >= self.long_seq_len:\n    # Process with transformer and extract trends/seasonality\n    hidden = torch.cat((short_term_hidden, trend_seasonality_hidden), dim=-1)\nelse:\n    # Only use short-term features\n    hidden = short_term_hidden\n```\n\n### 3. Adjacency Matrix Processing\n**Original**: Expects pre-computed support matrices\n**Adapted**: Converts LibCity\'s adj_mx to forward/backward transition matrices\n\n```python\ndef _prepare_supports(self):\n    # Forward: D^{-1} * A\n    # Backward: D^{-1} * A^T\n    return [adj_forward, adj_backward]\n```\n\n### 4. Loss Function Integration\n**Uses**: LibCity\'s `masked_mae_torch` with inverse scaling\n\n```python\ndef calculate_loss(self, batch):\n    y_true = batch[\'y\']\n    y_predicted = self.predict(batch)\n    y_true = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_true[..., :self.output_dim])\n    y_predicted = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_predicted[..., :self.output_dim])\n    return loss.masked_mae_torch(y_predicted, y_true, 0)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Recommendations\n\n### 1. Basic Import Test\n```bash\npython test_lsttn_import.py\n```\n\n### 2. Short-term Only Mode (Recommended for initial testing)\n```json\n{\n    "model": "LSTTN",\n    "dataset": "METR_LA",\n    "input_window": 12,\n    "output_window": 12,\n    "use_long_term": false,\n    "batch_size": 64\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Full Model with Long-term (Requires data preparation)\n```json\n{\n    "model": "LSTTN",\n    "dataset": "METR_LA",\n    "input_window": 4032,\n    "output_window": 12,\n    "use_long_term": true,\n    "batch_size": 16  # Smaller batch for memory\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n### 1. Long-term Data Requirement\n- Full model requires 4032 timesteps (14 days at 5-min intervals)\n- LibCity\'s default dataset loaders may not provide this much history\n- **Workaround**: Use `use_long_term=false` for standard datasets\n\n### 2. Pretrained Transformer\n- Original paper uses pretrained transformers\n- Not included in this adaptation\n- **Workaround**: Train from scratch or provide path via `pretrained_transformer_path`\n\n### 3. Memory Consumption\n- Full model (with long-term) is memory-intensive\n- **Recommendation**: Start with short-term only, use smaller batch sizes\n\n### 4. Graph Structure\n- Currently uses simple transition matrices\n- Could explore other normalization schemes in future\n\n---\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.pipeline import run_model\n\n# Run with default short-term mode\nrun_model(\n    task=\'traffic_state_pred\',\n    model=\'LSTTN\',\n    dataset=\'METR_LA\',\n    config_file=\'LSTTN_config.json\'\n)\n```\n\nOr with custom configuration:\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import LSTTN\nimport torch\n\nconfig = {\n    \'input_window\': 12,\n    \'output_window\': 12,\n    \'use_long_term\': False,\n    \'device\': torch.device(\'cuda\'),\n    # ... other parameters\n}\n\ndata_feature = {\n    \'num_nodes\': 207,\n    \'feature_dim\': 3,\n    \'output_dim\': 1,\n    \'adj_mx\': adj_matrix,\n    \'scaler\': scaler,\n}\n\nmodel = LSTTN(config, data_feature)\n\n# Training loop\nfor batch in dataloader:\n    loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n    loss.backward()\n    optimizer.step()\n```\n\n---\n\n## Migration Checklist\n\n- [x] Extract core model components from original implementation\n- [x] Adapt to LibCity\'s AbstractTrafficStateModel base class\n- [x] Implement required methods: `__init__`, `forward`, `predict`, `calculate_loss`\n- [x] Handle LibCity\'s batch format: `batch[\'X\']` and `batch[\'y\']`\n- [x] Integrate with LibCity\'s data_feature dictionary\n- [x] Process adjacency matrix appropriately\n- [x] Use LibCity\'s loss functions\n- [x] Support LibCity\'s scaler for inverse transform\n- [x] Register model in __init__.py\n- [x] Create test script\n- [x] Create configuration template\n- [x] Write comprehensive documentation\n- [x] Preserve original model logic and components\n\n---\n\n## Performance Notes\n\n### Expected Performance (based on original paper)\n- **METR-LA**: MAE ~2.8, RMSE ~5.5, MAPE ~7%\n- **PEMS-BAY**: MAE ~1.4, RMSE ~2.9, MAPE ~3%\n\n### Performance Factors\n1. **With Long-term Component**: Best performance, requires 14-day history\n2. **Short-term Only**: Good performance, works with standard input windows\n3. **Pretrained Transformer**: May improve long-term component accuracy\n4. **Adjacency Matrix**: Quality affects spatial modeling\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Import Errors\n```python\n# Ensure LibCity is in Python path\nimport sys\nsys.path.insert(0, \'/path/to/Bigscity-LibCity\')\n```\n\n### Memory Errors\n- Reduce batch_size\n- Disable long-term component: `use_long_term=false`\n- Use gradient checkpointing (future enhancement)\n\n### Shape Mismatches\n- Verify input_window matches configuration\n- Check num_nodes matches dataset\n- Ensure feature_dim is correct (usually 2 or 3)\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n### Immediate\n1. Run `test_lsttn_import.py` to verify installation\n2. Test with METR-LA dataset using short-term only mode\n3. Monitor training loss and validation metrics\n\n### Short-term\n1. Experiment with hyperparameters\n2. Compare short-term only vs. full model\n3. Benchmark